  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 929 PM CST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nOur next chance of rain will arrive Tuesday night into Wednesday \nmorning. Models aren't handling our PoPs well here in Middle TN and \nthis is likely due to inconsistencies in how the larger upper air \npattern is developing a tropical wave over Florida and off the east \ncoast on Wednesday. The GFS is trying to create a strong closed low \nover Arklatex at the same time and it's doing significantly \ndifferent things than what the Euro is suggesting. Either way, our \nchances of rain are going to be higher Wednesday morning through \nThursday, but the QPF is going to be the big question. In the end, \nthis mid-week system may only top out with an inch in some spots. \nMany will see less. Hopefully over the next 24 hours the QPF picture\nwill be a little clearer.\n\nBehind the rain ending on Thursday, it looks like we're in for \nanother extended period of dry weather along with temperatures \nmoderating back toward normal by the start of next week. This is the \ndirection the NBM has us leaning, but Euro solutions differ with \nadditional rains entering the picture by the end of next weekend.",
